{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00065",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.79,
      "end_seconds": 5.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.72,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.12,
      "end_seconds": 9.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Perfect, thanks. Hello there, so what's the trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 9.8,
      "end_seconds": 15.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "Doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.71,
      "end_seconds": 19.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 20.27,
      "end_seconds": 23.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "We came because of fever and chills."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.1,
      "end_seconds": 27.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.22,
      "end_seconds": 31.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "It's been going on for two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.04,
      "end_seconds": 39.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.65,
      "end_seconds": 49.81,
      "duration_seconds": 9.16,
      "text": "Paracetamol helps a bit. Moderate, I'd say. It sort of comes and goes. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 51.11,
      "end_seconds": 53.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.28,
      "end_seconds": 84.26,
      "duration_seconds": 28.98,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get a cough with phlegm as well. I've, I've had sharp pain on the right side when I breathe in too, for about two weeks. As for sharp pain on the right side when I breathe in, I'd say every other day. The cough with phlegm? That's been for about two weeks. I've also been feeling very weak, for about two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.9,
      "end_seconds": 89.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.61,
      "text": "Have you had fever and chills before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.66,
      "end_seconds": 96.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.29,
      "text": "Hmm, I had a similar thing a couple of years ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.68,
      "end_seconds": 103.81,
      "duration_seconds": 6.13,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any leg swelling, recent travel, vomiting or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 104.36,
      "end_seconds": 111.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.91,
      "text": "Oh, I haven't had leg swelling, recent travel, vomiting or coughing up blood, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.57,
      "end_seconds": 112.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Any palpitations or confusion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.61,
      "end_seconds": 117.53,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "No, you know, none of that at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.85,
      "end_seconds": 121.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "What about your tummy and bowels, anything unusual there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.25,
      "end_seconds": 124.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Nothing unusual, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.45,
      "end_seconds": 127.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.7,
      "end_seconds": 131.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.62,
      "text": "So, my father had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.63,
      "end_seconds": 138.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.98,
      "end_seconds": 144.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.97,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler, once a day. Ramipril. I take it 5 milligrams, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 145.26,
      "end_seconds": 153.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Um, doctor, I think the last prescription for the ramipril was 10 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.21,
      "end_seconds": 161.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "I see. Is the most recent prescription on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.54,
      "end_seconds": 165.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "No, I left it at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.04,
      "end_seconds": 170.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.56,
      "end_seconds": 176.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Oh, not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.68,
      "end_seconds": 178.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.95,
      "end_seconds": 184.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "No, never had any surgery."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.39,
      "end_seconds": 194.97,
      "duration_seconds": 6.58,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 195.84,
      "end_seconds": 202.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.62,
      "text": "I have COPD, for about ten years. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.03,
      "end_seconds": 205.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.15,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.22,
      "end_seconds": 211.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.36,
      "end_seconds": 212.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Okay. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.31,
      "end_seconds": 216.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.41,
      "text": "Okay, COPD, that's already on your record. Good to know."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 217.21,
      "end_seconds": 227.96,
      "duration_seconds": 10.75,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 139 over 84, pulse is 88 beats a minute. SpO2 92 percent on room air, temperature is 36.9 degrees, respiratory rate 20."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.15,
      "end_seconds": 229.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.83,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.2,
      "end_seconds": 233.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Can I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 235.08,
      "end_seconds": 236.07,
      "duration_seconds": 0.99,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.02,
      "end_seconds": 239.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.39,
      "end_seconds": 249.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Breathing rate is a bit fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.83,
      "end_seconds": 253.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.08,
      "end_seconds": 275.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "There's bronchial breathing and crackles at the right lower zone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 276.33,
      "end_seconds": 277.03,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.6,
      "end_seconds": 301.46,
      "duration_seconds": 20.86,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. So, based on the history and the examination, this looks most like a possible pneumonia on the right side. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. I can't rule out pleurisy yet. I'm going to order a sputum culture, for pneumonia. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.42,
      "end_seconds": 305.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Right, alright. When can I do that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.47,
      "end_seconds": 315.22,
      "duration_seconds": 8.75,
      "text": "Let's get a chest X-ray, for suspected pneumonia. We should do blood tests for infection. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 316.72,
      "end_seconds": 321.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "Um, sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.09,
      "end_seconds": 333.67,
      "duration_seconds": 11.58,
      "text": "Let's use levofloxacin, 500 milligrams, once a day, for five days. It's for chest infection. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 334.68,
      "end_seconds": 338.94,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Okay, uh, and I take that after food?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.86,
      "end_seconds": 365.86,
      "duration_seconds": 26.0,
      "text": "I'll start you on paracetamol, 500 milligrams, every six hours if needed, for three days. It's for fever and body aches. I'll put all of this in writing so you don't have to remember it. Rest and fluids, and finish every dose of the antibiotic. Try to get to bed and wake up at the same time each day, and keep your phone away from the bed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 366.85,
      "end_seconds": 373.58,
      "duration_seconds": 6.73,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 374.81,
      "end_seconds": 376.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.29,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.46,
      "end_seconds": 387.43,
      "duration_seconds": 10.97,
      "text": "Keep an eye out, and if the breathlessness worsens or you become drowsy, call us the same day or go to emergency. Please come and see me after the X-ray."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 388.44,
      "end_seconds": 390.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "So, okay, I'll book that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 392.1,
      "end_seconds": 394.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 395.5,
      "end_seconds": 398.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 401.55,
      "end_seconds": 402.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Take care."
    }
  ]
}